    "url": "https://job-boards.eu.greenhouse.io/tripledotstudios/jobs/4954095101",
    "desc": "Who are we?\n\nTripledot Studios is one of the largest independent mobile games companies in the world.\n\nWe are a multi-award-winning organisation, with a global 2,500+ strong team across 12 studios.\n\nOur expanded portfolio includes some of the biggest titles in mobile gaming, collectively reaching top chart positions around the world and engaging over 25 million daily active users.\n\nTripledot’s guiding principle is that when people love what they do, what they do will be loved by others.\n\nWe’re building a company we’re proud of. One filled with driven, incredibly smart and detail-orientated people, who LOVE making games.\n\nOur ambition is to be the most successful games company in the world, and we’re just getting started.\n\nThis role will be working at Lion Studios\n\nLion Studios is a mobile games publisher that works with mobile developers to get their games discovered by players around the world. Headquartered in San Francisco, Lion Studios’ creative and strategy teams utilize their expertise to help game developers break through the noise and grow their businesses.\n\nSince launching in 2018, Lion Studios has driven 90% of its games to the Top 10 in the App Store and Google Play and helped drive 16 games to #1 in the US App Store’s Top Free chart.\n\nRole Overview\n\nAs a Market Intelligence Analyst, you will help Lion Studios to identify opportunities in the mobile games market and turn market signals into practical recommendations. You will track competitor launches and releases, analyse product and growth strategies, and identify underserved or fast-growing areas that could shape Lion’s pipeline and growth.\n\nThis is a hands-on, cross-functional role working closely with partner studios, studio management, game designers, product stakeholders, and the creative team. You will contribute from early-stage ideation through execution, using research and critical thinking to help teams make stronger product decisions.\n\nYou will thrive in this role if you combine strong game design judgement with an entrepreneurial mindset, can work autonomously, and enjoy moving from analysis to clear, actionable ideas.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n• Track competitor launches, releases, product changes, and market activity to understand where competitors are placing their bets.\n• Identify emerging trends, underserved audiences, and areas of the mobile games market that are gaining momentum.\n• Translate market signals into actionable recommendations for Lion’s product pipeline and growth strategy.\n• Conduct competitor and market analyses to understand product, game design, creative, and growth strategies.\n• Support partner studios from ideation through execution by contributing market context, game insights, and opportunity assessments.\n• Prepare and share clear reports, game analyses, and product deconstructions with relevant stakeholders.\n• Work cross-functionally with studio managers, game designers, product stakeholders, and creative teams.\n• Build strong working relationships with a group of partner studios and adapt your focus as team and product needs evolve.\n• Explore ways to exploit AI to make research, analysis, execution, and recurring workflows more effective.\n\nRequired Skills, Knowledge and Expertise\n\n• 3+ years of relevant experience in market research, market intelligence, game design, product strategy, marketing strategy, or a related analytical role.\n• Strong game design sense and the ability to assess why game concepts, mechanics, and market opportunities may succeed.\n• Experience interpreting market and competitor data and turning it into clear insights and practical next steps.\n• Strong critical thinking skills, with the ability to form point of views.\n• An entrepreneurial mindset and the ability to spot underserved opportunities and propose ways to act on them.\n• Strong communication skills and the ability to present analysis clearly to both creative and commercial stakeholders.\n\nDesired Skills\n\n• Experience in mobile gaming, ideally within a studio that regularly takes games from ideation to launch and responds quickly to market trends.\n• Experience in app publishing or another fast-moving consumer product environment may also be relevant when paired with strong market analysis and product judgement.\n• Familiarity with AI tools is a plus; a willingness to learn and apply them is important.\n\nWorking at Tripledot\n\n• 25 days holiday: Enjoy 25 days of paid holiday, in addition to bank holidays to relax and refresh throughout the year.\n• Continuous Professional Development: Propel your career with continuous opportunities for professional development.\n• Supplemental Health Insurance: Continentale: annual budget of 1200 eur - reimbursement for healthcare outside of public plans (glasses, massages, dental treatments etc.)\n• Public Transportation reimbursement: 100% of public transportation to the office via BVG ticket is covered\n• Daily Free Lunch: Order free food from Wolt when at the office\n• Pension plan: Opt-in to employer contributed pension plan, operated with Degura",
