    "url": "https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/wargamingen/jobs/8125576",
    "desc": "Job Overview\n\nWe are looking for a Project Manager to join the World of Tanks: Modern Armor team and support the development of our console game. This role will focus on coordinating multiple areas of game development, including Art, Design, Engineering, QA, and other cross-functional teams, ensuring that projects and initiatives are delivered smoothly and effectively.\n\nThe Project Manager will work closely with Producer, Product Manager, and cross-functional teams to coordinate workflows, manage priorities, identify and mitigate risks, and ensure alignment across different development pipelines.\n\nWhat will you do?\n\n• Create and maintain project plans aligned with the team roadmap, ensuring a strong sense of ownership and accountability for each team member’s contributions\n• Help the Producer lead a team consisting of designers, developers, QA specialists, and artists\n• Set and monitor key delivery milestones for each project plan, and define, together with the team, the artifacts required to successfully complete them\n• Work on scope prioritization together with the Producer and other team members\n• Take part in greenlight meetings with stakeholders and prepare presentations\n• Provide regular reports on team progress, including risks and mitigation plans, to multiple levels of management\n• Be ready to improve processes both at the team and overall development level\n• Help balance workloads across departments\n• Coordinate regular team activities and help remove roadblocks at any stage of roadmap development\n\nWhat are we looking for?\n\n• 4+ years of experience managing production activities within international teams\n• Proven ability to manage large-scale projects and different pipelines, including art\n• Solid understanding of and experience implementing project management methodologies (e.g., Agile, Waterfall), risk management best practices, and scope prioritization tools\n• Extensive knowledge of tech pipelines, DLC, and related terminology\n• Hands-on experience with JIRA, MS Project, or other project management tools\n• Proven ability to effectively collaborate across teams involved in the development cycle\n• Strong communication skills in English (written and spoken)\n\nWhat additional skills will help you stand out?\n\n• Previous experience working with art teams, processes, or pipelines\n• Experience working with large, cross-functional development teams\n• Experience in the game industry (console)\n• Passion for video games\n\nWork mode\n\n• Hybrid (2-3 days of work from the office)\n• This role is eligible for relocation & immigration support\n\nThe salary range for this role in Vilnius is EUR 4000-6500 monthly gross.\n\nBenefits\n\nBenefits and perks are tailored to the local market and culture. Our benefits in Vilnius include:\n\n• Additional paid time off\n• Sick Leave Compensation\n• Pregnancy and Childbirth Leave Benefit\n• Career development and education opportunities within the company\n• Meal Allowance\n• Premium Private Health Care\n• Mental well-being program (iFeel)\n• Perks discounts platform (over 450 exclusive discounts)\n• Personal Gaming Account\n• Coffee, fruits, and snacks in the office\n• Company events\n• Seniority Awards\n• Referral program - You can recommend the best talents to the company and receive a reward\n\nPlease submit your CV in English to ensure smooth processing and review.\nAbout Wargaming\n\nWargaming is an award-winning online game developer and publisher headquartered in Nicosia, Cyprus. Operating since 1998, Wargaming has become one of the leaders in the gaming industry with 15 offices worldwide, including studios in Chicago, Prague, Shanghai, Tokyo, and Vilnius. Our diverse and multicultural team works together to deliver a top-class experience to millions of players who enjoy Wargaming's titles across all major gaming platforms. Our flagship products include free-to-play hits World of Tanks, World of Warships and World of Tanks Blitz.\n\nPlease see Wargaming Candidate Privacy Policy for details on how Wargaming uses your personal data.",
