    "desc": "Who We Are\n\n2K is headquartered in Novato, California and is a wholly owned label of Take-Two Interactive Software, Inc. (NASDAQ: TTWO). Founded in 2005, 2K Games is a global video game company, publishing titles developed by some of the most influential game development studios in the world. Our studios responsible for developing 2K’s portfolio of world-class games across multiple platforms, include Visual Concepts, Firaxis, Hangar 13, CatDaddy, Cloud Chamber, 31st Union, HB Studios, and 2K SportsLab. Our portfolio of titles is expanding due to our global strategic plan, building and acquiring exciting studios whose content continues to inspire all of us! 2K publishes titles in today’s most popular gaming genres, including sports, shooters, action, role-playing, strategy, casual, and family entertainment.\n\nOur team of engineers, marketers, artists, writers, data scientists, producers, thinkers and doers, are the professional publishing stewards of 2K’s portfolio currently includes several AAA, sports and entertainment brands, including global powerhouse NBA®️ 2K, renowned BioShock®️, Borderlands®️, Mafia, Sid Meier’s Civilization®️ and XCOM®️ brands; popular WWE®️ 2K and WWE®️ SuperCard franchises, TopSpin 2K25, as well as the critically and commercially acclaimed PGA TOUR®️ 2K\n\nAt 2K, we pride ourselves on creating an inclusive work environment, which means encouraging our teams to Come as You Are and do your best work! We encourage ALL applicants to explore our global positions, even if they don’t meet every requirement for the role. If you're interested in the job and think you have what it takes to work at 2K, we encourage you to apply!\n\nWhat We Need\n\nWe are seeking a DevOps Engineer who can build, support, and improve infrastructure, CI/CD pipelines, and operational tooling that help teams deliver reliable services and better developer experience. This role focuses on hands-on engineering, automation, and day-to-day operational excellence in partnership with other engineers and teams.\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\n• Build and maintain CI/CD pipelines, cloud infrastructure, and deployment automation.\n• Support the reliability, scalability, and performance of development and production environments.\n• Improve developer workflows through automation, tooling, and documentation.\n• Contribute to observability efforts, including monitoring, alerting, dashboards, and incident response.\n• Partner with software engineers and platform teams to troubleshoot issues and improve delivery processes.\n• Participate in on-call rotations and help resolve operational incidents.\n• Help maintain infrastructure standards, security practices, and operational runbooks.\n• Support cost-conscious engineering through efficient infrastructure usage and tagging practices.\n\nWhat Will Make You a Great Fit\n\n• 4+ years of experience in DevOps, SRE, or Platform Engineering roles within an enterprise or multi-team environment.\n• Hands-on experience with production cloud infrastructure (AWS or GCP) and containerized/orchestration platforms (e.g., Kubernetes/EKS).\n• Experience with Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC) workflows (e.g., Terraform) and managing environment-specific configurations.\n• Experience building or maintaining CI/CD pipelines using platforms such as GitHub Actions or Jenkins.\n• Demonstrated operational experience, including participating in on-call rotations, managing production incidents, and using observability tools (e.g., Datadog, Splunk, Grafana).\n• Familiarity with managing work via formal ticketing systems (e.g., Jira, ServiceNow) and cross-functional coordination.\n• A focus on service reliability, documentation (runbooks), and operational excellence.\n• Strong troubleshooting and analytical skills, with a proven ability to identify root causes and work collaboratively across diverse engineering teams.\n• Clear and effective communication skills, particularly in conveying technical information, documenting processes, and adapting to fast-paced environments. Bonus Points\n• Experience supporting GitOps-based deployment workflows and tools such as ArgoCD.\n• Familiarity with cost optimization practices, including tagging strategies, rightsizing, and resource usage analysis.\n• Exposure to security-focused automation, such as secrets management, policy enforcement, or vulnerability/scanning workflows.\n• Experience writing scripts or lightweight tooling in languages such as Python, Bash, or Go.\n\nWhat we offer you:\n\n• Great Company Culture. We pride ourselves as being one of the most creative and innovative places to work, creativity, innovation, efficiency, diversity and philanthropy are among the core tenets of our organization and are integral drivers of our continued success.\n• Growth: As a global entertainment company, we pride ourselves on creating environments where employees are encouraged to be themselves, inquisitive, collaborative and to grow within and around the company.\n• Work Hard, Enjoy Life. Our employees’ bond, blow-off steam, and flex some creative muscles – through corporate boot camp classes, company parties, our Office gaming spaces, game release events, monthly socials, and team challenges.\n• Benefits. Benefits include, but are not limited to; Discretionary bonus, Provident fund contributions, 1+5 medical insurance + top up options and access to Practo online Doctor consultation App, Employee assistance program, 3X CTC Life Assurance, 3X CTC Personal accident insurance, childcare services, 20 days holiday + statutory holidays,\n• Perks. Gym reimbursement up to INR1150 per month, wellbeing program with the chance to earn up to $93 per annum, charitable giving program, access to learning platforms, employee discount program’s plus free games and events!…",
