    "desc": "ABOUT VOODOO\n\nFounded in 2013, Voodoo is a tech company that creates mobile games and apps with a mission to entertain the world. Gathering 800 employees, 7 billion downloads, and over 200 million active users, Voodoo is the #3 mobile publisher worldwide in terms of downloads after Google and Meta. Our portfolio includes chart-topping games like Mob Control and Block Jam, alongside popular apps such as BeReal and Wizz. \n\nThis position is Istanbul-based.\n\n\n\n\nTEAM\n\nYou will be an integral part of a newly established internal studio, a dynamic and focused team dedicated to one of our most promising prototype in scale. This studio is specifically chartered to improve this high-potential game up to the successful and market-ready title it is meant to become. \n\n\n\n\nROLE\n\nWe’re seeking a talented and seasoned Game Designer who is deeply passionate about Puzzle games and laser-focused on creating the next big hit. With extensive experience in the industry, you'll play a pivotal role in delivering fun to millions of players. As the driving force behind the game's success, you'll ensure the game reaches the highest standards of quality and innovation.\n\n - Define a clear, cohesive design pipeline\n\n - Pitch and implement big features to the team, deconstructing them into smaller components\n\n - Own game balancing, pace, feel\n\n - Always back up your ideas with available data points\n\n - Ability to deconstruct and analyze mobile games mechanics\n\n - Get involved in all aspects of game development: UI, UX, Game Design, logic, performance, etc. \n\n - Fine-tune game balancing, pacing, and feel\n\n - Benchmark the market to stay on top of new trends\n\n - Understanding of models and tools to analyze gameplay and user behavior\n\n - Proficiency in Unity a huge plus\n\n - Familiarity with Figma or similar visual collaboration software\n\n - Able to create a playable prototype individually as well as within a team\n   \n   \n\n\nPROFILE\n\n - At least 5 years of professional experience in Game Development and at least 3 years as a game designer\n\n - Experience working on mobile games, F2P or RPG\n\n - Experience in designing LiveOps for a live product is a huge plus\n\n - Creative and hacker mindset\n\n - Good sense of gameplay experience, and special attention to detail\n\n - Communication skills in English, both written and verbal\n\n - Knowledge of casual games\n\n - Deep collaboration mindset, including excellent interpersonal and communication skills, and a positive mindset towards receiving, acting on, and giving feedback\n\n - Accountability, independence, and responsibility when given ownership over your work\n\n - An eagerness to learn new ways to perform your tasks in a more efficient way, and to improve yourself day after day\n   \n   \n\n\nBENEFITS: \n\n - Best in Class compensation\n\n - Other benefits according to the country you reside.",
