    "posted": "2026-07-15",
    "url": "https://jobs.lever.co/xsolla/31587df5-85ff-47ec-914c-ee0d51f1e123",
    "desc": "About You\n\nWe’re looking for a Web3 Fullstack Engineer to build the layer where web2 and web3 meet. Our mission is seamless web2 ↔ web3 integration — letting players and developers interact with digital items and move them through their full lifecycle (mint, own, trade, transfer, redeem, retire) without ever having to think about which side of the chain they’re on. You’ll work across the whole stack: wallet-connected frontends, high-throughput backend services, and the smart contract and indexing layers that make on-chain items feel as fast and familiar as anything in web2.\n\nThis is a hands-on engineering role with broad ownership. A player buying an item with a credit card, a game granting an in-game asset, and a marketplace settling a peer-to-peer trade should all resolve to the same coherent item model — regardless of whether the item lives in a database, a custodial wallet, or on-chain. Making that experience invisible to the end user, and reliable for the developer, is the core of the job.\n\nYou care about product quality and developer experience as much as protocol correctness. You’re comfortable owning a feature end to end, reasoning about trust and custody boundaries, and making pragmatic calls about what belongs on-chain versus off-chain.\n\nAbout Us\n\nXsolla is a global commerce company with robust tools and services to help developers solve the inherent challenges of the video game industry. From indie to AAA, companies partner with Xsolla to help them fund, distribute, market, and monetize their games. Grounded in the belief in the future of video games, Xsolla is resolute in the mission to bring opportunities together, and continually make new resources available to creators. Headquartered and incorporated in Los Angeles, California, Xsolla operates as the merchant of record and has helped over 1,500+ game developers to reach more players and grow their businesses around the world. With more paths to profits and ways to win, developers have all the things needed to enjoy the game.\n\nFor more information, visit xsolla.com\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\nBuild Seamless Web2 ↔ Web3 Integration — Design and ship the flows that let users move between traditional accounts/payments and on-chain wallets without friction: custodial and non-custodial wallets, account abstraction, gasless transactions, and fiat on-ramps.\n\nOwn the Digital Item Lifecycle — Build the systems behind item mint, ownership, transfer, trading, and redemption — keeping on-chain state and off-chain records consistent, auditable, and fast.\n\nDevelop Fullstack Features — Deliver end to end across wallet-connected frontends, backend services, and the smart contract / indexing layer that powers item ownership and turnover.\n\nModel Items & Ownership — Design data models and APIs that represent items uniformly whether they live off-chain, in a custodial wallet, or on-chain, and keep them in sync.\n\nEnsure Reliability of Value Flows — Anything that moves items or money must be correct under failure: idempotency, reconciliation, replay safety, and clear recovery paths.\n\nIntegrate Blockchains & Marketplaces — Interact with EVM chains, token standards, indexers, and marketplace/settlement flows; abstract their differences behind clean internal interfaces.\n\nCollaborate Across Teams — Work with product, security, payments, and game-facing teams to turn business needs into well-scoped technical plans, and document decisions so they stand on their own.\n\nWHAT YOU BRING\nWeb3 & Digital Assets\n\nWeb2 ↔ Web3 Integration — Hands-on experience bridging traditional systems with on-chain ones: wallet onboarding, custodial vs. non-custodial trade-offs, account abstraction, gasless/relayed transactions.\n\nEVM & Smart Contracts — Working knowledge of EVM chains and Solidity, including reading, integrating with, and reasoning about the safety of contracts.\n\nToken & Item Standards — Practical understanding of ERC-20, ERC-721, and ERC-1155, and how they map to real game items, ownership, and transfers.\n\nOn-chain / Off-chain Sync — Experience keeping blockchain state consistent with off-chain databases: indexing, event ingestion, reorg handling, and reconciliation.\n\nFrontend Engineering\n\nTypeScript & React — Strong TypeScript and React skills for building responsive, production-grade interfaces.\n\nWallet Integration — Experience with wallet connectivity and web3 client libraries (e.g. wagmi, viem, ethers.js, WalletConnect) and embedded/social login wallets.\n\nBackend Engineering\n\nBackend Services — Solid backend skills in Node.js and Go: clean APIs, concurrency, and performance under load.\n\nDistributed Systems — Experience with distributed systems and their trade-offs (consistency, availability, failure modes), especially where correctness of value transfer matters.\n\nData & Infrastructure\n\nPostgreSQL — Schema design, query optimization, and migrations at scale.\n\nKubernetes — Deploying, operating, and debugging services in a k8s environment.\n\nMessage Streaming — Kafka or NATS — event-driven patterns, consumer groups, at-least-once delivery.\n\nGit & CI/CD — Git and modern CI/CD practices.\n\nDomain Context\n\nGaming Industry Experience — Experience building or operating platforms for game developers, publishers, or players — especially anything touching in-game items, economies, or ownership.\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n• Experience building NFT marketplaces, item trading, or secondary-market / settlement systems\n• Familiarity with blockchain indexing tooling (The Graph, custom indexers) and node/RPC infrastructure\n• Experience with account abstraction (ERC-4337), smart wallets, or paymaster/relayer setups\n• Background in payments or fiat on-ramp integration bridging traditional commerce and crypto\n• Experience with non-EVM ecosystems (Solana, etc.) or cross-chain / bridging patterns\n• Familiarity with security and compliance relevant to digital assets: custody, key management, audit logging, KYC/AML touchpoints\n• Contributions to open-source web3, wallet, or tooling projects\n• Hands-on,",
