    "desc": "ABOUT US\n\nXsolla is a global commerce company with robust tools and services to help developers solve the inherent challenges of the video game industry. From indie to AAA, companies partner with Xsolla to help them fund, distribute, market, and monetize their games. Grounded in the belief in the future of video games, Xsolla is resolute in the mission to bring opportunities together, and continually make new resources available to creators. Headquartered and incorporated in Los Angeles, California, Xsolla operates as the merchant of record and has helped over 1,500+ game developers to reach more players and grow their businesses around the world. With more paths to profits and ways to win, developers have all the things needed to enjoy the game.\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n• Own end-to-end IT onboarding and offboarding, including account setup, access provisioning and deprovisioning, and equipment handoff.\n• Administer the company's core internal and external services (Google Workspace, Atlassian, Okta, LDAP, VPN, SIP), along with the office network and AV and conference-room systems.\n• Act as the primary on-site point of contact for the office, providing a mix of on-site and remote support with a strong customer-service focus.\n• Manage office IT equipment across its full lifecycle: procurement, deployment, maintenance, and decommissioning of hardware (printers and scanners, peripherals, AV) and software, keeping the asset inventory accurate and all allocations logged.\n• Own vendor relationships for IT hardware and services (for example, Apple, Dell, Asus, Logitech).\n• Provide IT support for internal events such as meet-ups and conferences, and support employee desk moves and office reconfigurations.\n• Create and maintain clear IT documentation and runbooks for the systems and processes you own.\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n• At least 3 to 4 years of hands-on IT experience covering hardware and software troubleshooting, installation, and maintenance.\n• Professional working proficiency in English, with the ability to explain technical concepts clearly to non-technical colleagues.\n• Hands-on experience administering core business and identity systems (for example, Google Workspace, Atlassian, Okta, LDAP, VPN).\n• Experience with office networking, AV and conference-room systems, CCTV and physical security systems, and backup and recovery.\n• Excellent interpersonal skills with a genuine customer-service mindset.\n• Comfortable working independently and owning problems end to end in a dynamic environment where priorities can shift quickly.\n• Proactive and organized, eager to learn, with strong practical problem-solving skills.\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n• Experience supporting a global or multi-office organization.\n• Previous work experience at a fast-paced organization with an entrepreneurial mindset.\n• Associate's or Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field.\n• Additional language skills, such as Azerbaijani or Russian.\nThe duties and responsibilities of this position may evolve over time to support the organization’s goals and individual growth. This job description is intended to outline the general nature and level of work being performed and is not intended to be an exhaustive list of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications required. By submitting your application, you consent to Xsolla conducting background checks, where permitted by law, after the final interview stage. All checks will comply with local regulations, and your information will be handled confidentially. Xsolla takes your privacy seriously and will not sell or externally distribute any personal data received during the hiring process. In accordance with applicable data protection laws, Xsolla is committed to protecting your personal information and respecting your privacy.\n\nFor any inquiries related to data privacy, please contact: careers@xsolla.com\n\nExplore more opportunities at: https://xsolla.com/careers",
