    "desc": "With multiple awards to our name, Larian Studios has proven that we’re dedicated to delivering high-quality role-playing games. As we move on to new projects, the studio that brought you Baldur’s Gate 3 & Divinity: Original Sin 2 is looking for a Gameplay Programming Intern to join the team and help us in crafting the high caliber games our fans have come to expect.\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n• Solid knowledge of C++\n• Strong understanding of basic C++ concepts (types, OOP, memory management, etc.)\n• Ability to write robust code without infinite loops or memory leaks\n• Portfolio of personal C++ project(s) (with source code), not older than 2 years\n• Projects must be personal work (university coursework will not be considered)\n• Applications without coding examples will not be considered\n• Open-minded and willing to experiment and iterate on features\n• Good communication skills in English\n• Passion for making and playing great games\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n• Collaborate with developers on real gameplay systems\n• Actively participate in game production as part of the technical creative team\n• Design, develop, and support gameplay systems for the RPG (including code architecture)\n• Work on all aspects of gameplay system implementation\n• Cooperate closely with other departments to implement required game components\n• Collaborate with UI designers to implement in-game UI features\n• Write robust, maintainable, and high-quality code\nWe are looking for highly motivated individuals with ever-evolving skillsets and passion for player experience. If you want to contribute to making amazing RPG experiences, we would love to hear from you.",
