    "url": "https://jobs.lever.co/amanotes/01540a47-eed9-4b9b-9de9-a91658f76aa3",
    "desc": "\nOBJECTIVES\n• Tiles Hop, Dancing Road, and Magic Tiles 3 is a top-ranked music games with a passionate global audience. As a Senior Product Owner – LiveOps, you will play a pivotal role in shaping and growing games that have already reached millions of players globally. This role is for someone who’s not only passionate about games, but also thrives in data-driven decision-making, rapid experimentation, and cross-functional collaboration. You’ll be empowered to define the product vision, own the roadmap, and drive performance across retention, monetization, and user satisfaction.\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\nProduct Ownership:\n\n• Define and own the roadmap for key features or game areas, ensuring alignment with product goals.\n• Write detailed user stories and acceptance criteria, and manage the backlog to prioritize the highest-impact features.\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams to ensure features are implemented on time and at a high quality.\n\nGame Development & Strategy:\n\n• Work closely with the Product Manager to shape the overall game vision and strategy.\n• Contribute to designing innovative gameplay loops, hybrid monetization systems, and engagement mechanics.\n• Act as a mentor to Junior Product Owners and other team members, providing guidance and support.\n\nData-Driven Decision Making:\n\n• Use analytics and player feedback to inform decisions and optimize features for retention, engagement, and monetization.\n• Collaborate with the analytics team to design and evaluate A/B tests for new features and updates.\n• Identify key metrics and set success criteria for features and updates.\n\nLiveOps & Player Engagement:\n\n• Help plan and execute LiveOps strategies, including events, seasonal updates, and new content releases.\n• Partner with marketing teams to align player acquisition and retention initiatives with product goals.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n• 5+ years of experience in product ownership, product management, or a related role in the gaming industry.\n• Self-starter who is energetic, confident, adaptable, and player-focused\n• Experience supporting or owning live features for mobile games—rhythm or hybrid-casual titles a plus\n• Demonstrated use of data, experimentation, and player feedback to boost product engagement or monetisation\n• Ability to produce wireframes, mock-ups, prototypes, and user-interaction diagrams (Figma, Miro, etc.)\n• Comfortable querying and visualising data to answer product questions\n• Solid Agile/Scrum skills: you write crisp user stories and acceptance criteria and can guide a sprint from planning to release\n• Excellent written and spoken English; strong problem-solving and presentation abilities\n• Nice to have:\n• Familiarity with AI-powered tools to boost productivity and creativity\n• Passion for music and rhythm games—enough to spot a good beat map or suggest music-driven event ideas.\n• Understanding of F2P economies, core-loop and progression design, and live-ops best practices\n\nOUR CULTURE:\n\n• We believe in rapid iteration, honest feedback, and celebrating every win. You’ll find autonomy, supportive peers, and the chance to impact millions of players with your work. If crafting joyful, music-powered experiences excites you, we’d love to meet. Ready to join the beat? Send us your CV and a short note about a data-driven product success you’re proud of.\n\nBENEFITS\nAt Amanotes, you will be enjoying the dynamic working environment with unique music culture many benefits as below:\n\n• Competitive salary upon experience\n• 13th-month salary\n• Annual Performance Bonus\n• Flexible working time\n• Personal learning and well-being budget\n• Team-building budget\n• Lunch and parking allowance\n• Various learning activities, including internal training & sharing, international conferences, and e-learning (Udemy, Linkedin Learning...)\n• Engaging music events: Music Night, Amasing Night, Music schools…\n• Employee Assistance Program to support mental health & well-being\n• Minimum 12 days of paid annual leave, plus 10 days of paid sick leave\n• 12 days working from home per year\n• Attractive relocation package (for several positions)\nConsent Notice for Personal Data Processing\n- By applying to any position at Amanotes, you acknowledge and agree that your personal data will be collected and processed for recruitment-related purposes. Please read the “Consent Notice for Personal Data Processing” carefully before submitting your application.\n- Thank you for your interest in joining Amanotes.\n\nAbout Amanotes\n\nWe are Amanotes – a dynamic music game company that’s using cutting-edge technology to transform how people experience music.\n\nSince 2014, we’ve led the global simple music game market with over 3.5 billion downloads across 190+ countries, including chart-topping titles like Magic Tiles 3, Tiles Hop, Dancing Road, and Duet Cats.\n\nAs the #1 Music Game Publisher worldwide and the #1 App Publisher from Southeast Asia by downloads, our ambition is clear: to create iconic, hybrid-casual music games that people love and play for years.\n\nWhat truly sets Amanotes apart is not just what we build — it’s how we grow and who we grow with:\n\n🎓 We invest in your growth through learning budgets, coaching, and stretch opportunities.\n\n🎶 We embrace a creative and dynamic culture, where everyone can play, share, and thrive.\n\n🧘 We believe in work-life harmony — your rhythm matters here.\n\n🏆 We recognize and reward impact, with competitive benefits and clear development paths.\n\nCome join our music-filled workplace, where innovation meets rhythm — and let’s create a magical music experience together.\n\nAmanotes – Where Everyone Can Music.\n\nHow To Apply?\n\nClick the button or contact us at talents@amanotes.com.",
