    "url": "https://careers.reality.co/o/junior-qa-intern",
    "desc": "We're gearing up for something big - Monopoly World is going global! This is your chance to be part of an exciting, high-impact project that will reach players all around the world. 🌍\n\nIf you're looking for an opportunity to level up your career, work with an amazing team, and add a truly standout experience to your portfolio, this is it!\n\nCome build something incredible with us! Check out our trailer and see what’s in store! 🚀🎥\n\nLooking for a way to kickstart your career in mobile game development? Our Junior QA Intern position is the perfect opportunity for you! As a Junior QA Intern, you'll learn the ropes of game testing and quality assurance from experienced professionals. You'll get hands-on experience with industry-standard tools, develop and execute test plans, and learn how to report and track bugs. The ideal candidate should have a basic understanding of software development, and be currently enrolled in a degree program in Computer Science, Game Design, or a related field. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, as well as excellent communication skills, are a must.\n\nThis role will report to the Head of Production. It’s a full-time position located in our office in Cracow, Poland.\n\nAs a Junior QA Intern, you will have the opportunity to work closely with our experienced team to ensure the quality and functionality of our games.\n\n• Assist in testing new features and functionalities of our games\n• Identify and report bugs and issues\n• Collaborate with developers and designers to improve game quality\n• Learn and apply testing methodologies and best practices\n• Contribute to the overall success of our game development process\n\nIf you are passionate about gaming, have a keen eye for detail, and are eager to learn and grow in the field of QA testing, we would love to hear from you. This internship will provide valuable hands-on experience and the opportunity to work on exciting projects in the gaming industry.\n\nBasic Responsibilities\n\n• Perform Black Box testing\n• Analyzing specifications\n• Implementing and executing test plans\n• Report bugs",
