    "salary": null,
    "posted": "2022-08-19",
    "url": "https://jobs.lever.co/amanotes/284789f4-a83e-4727-9738-211cdfbe8201",
    "desc": "\nOBJECTIVES\n• Amanotes is seeking a Playable Ads Developer who can provide users with an engaging and interactive gameplay experience. Playable ads are designed to be opt-in, true to the nature of the game, and provide users with an immersive and enjoyable ad experience.\n• In this role, you will be responsible for converting existing games into playable games. To be successful, you will need to create a compelling gaming demo experience that appeals to a broad audience.\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n• Explore and expand playable ad development beyond Unity/Luna by evaluating and implementing web-based approaches such as Cocos Creator, Phaser or PixiJS with TypeScript/JavaScript.\n• Design reusable, modular and data-driven playable templates that support rapid asset, level, theme and endcard customization without rewriting core gameplay logic.\n• Build automation-ready workflows for asset replacement, level/config generation, batch variant creation, build packaging, preview generation and technical QA across playable ad networks.\n• Develop and maintain lightweight HTML5 playable builds using web tooling such as Node.js/npm and Webpack, Vite or equivalent bundlers, while optimizing asset size, runtime performance and responsive behavior.\n• Integrate lifecycle, CTA and custom tracking events for A/B testing, and troubleshoot platform, SDK and ad-network-specific issues.\n• Lead technical explorations, code reviews and documentation standards, and mentor other playable developers on multi-stack development, performance optimization and automation.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\nExperience:\n\n• Advanced experience with Unity/C# and Luna or a comparable playable ads production workflow.\n• Strong experience with at least one web game/playable framework, such as Cocos Creator, Phaser or PixiJS, using TypeScript and/or JavaScript.\n• Solid understanding of HTML5, CSS responsive layout, Canvas/WebGL, mobile browser behavior, touch input and device orientation.\n• Experience with Node.js/npm, Webpack, Vite or equivalent tooling for bundling and shipping lightweight HTML5 builds.\n• Experience designing reusable templates and data/config-driven gameplay systems for rapid iteration and variant production.\n• Experience building automation or internal tools for asset processing, level/config generation, batch builds, technical validation, QA or publishing workflows.\n• Strong knowledge of performance and build-size optimization, including image/audio compression, texture atlases, minification and runtime profiling.\n• Experience integrating SDKs, CTA/lifecycle events, analytics or ad-network-specific requirements is highly valued.\n• Able to use Python, JavaScript/TypeScript or shell scripting to automate repetitive development and production tasks.\n• Strong plus: PixiJS, WebGL shaders, CI/CD, no-code parameterization, AI-assisted development, SALA/Snapbeat or similar automation systems.\n\nSoft skills:\n\n• We are looking for a teammate who is hardworking, collaborative, and passionate about games.\n• Naturally curious and always looking for new ways to solve problems.\n• Enjoy working in a fast-paced environment and are able to learn quickly.\n• Ambitious and always seeking opportunities to grow and improve.\n\nBENEFITS\nAt Amanotes, you will be enjoying the dynamic working environment with unique music culture many benefits as below:\n\n• Competitive salary upon experience\n• 13th month salary\n• Annual Performance Bonus\n• Game Incentive\n• Flexible working time\n• Personal learning and well-being budget\n• Team-building budget\n• Lunch and parking allowance\n• Various learning activities, including internal training & sharing, international conferences, and e-learning (Udemy, Linkedin Learning...)\n• Engaging music events: Music Night, Amasing Night, Music schools…\n• Employee Assistance Program to support mental health & well-being\n• 12 days of paid annual leave, plus 10 days of paid sick leave\n• 12 days working from home per year\n• Attractive relocation package (for several positions)\nConsent Notice for Personal Data Processing\n- By applying to any position at Amanotes, you acknowledge and agree that your personal data will be collected and processed for recruitment-related purposes. Please read the “Consent Notice for Personal Data Processing” carefully before submitting your application.\n- Thank you for your interest in joining Amanotes.\n\nAbout Amanotes\n\nWe are Amanotes – a dynamic music game company that’s using cutting-edge technology to transform how people experience music.\n\nSince 2014, we’ve led the global simple music game market with over 3.5 billion downloads across 190+ countries, including chart-topping titles like Magic Tiles 3, Tiles Hop, Dancing Road, and Duet Cats.\n\nAs the #1 Music Game Publisher worldwide and the #1 App Publisher from Southeast Asia by downloads, our ambition is clear: to create iconic, hybrid-casual music games that people love and play for years.\n\nWhat truly sets Amanotes apart is not just what we build — it’s how we grow and who we grow with:\n\n🎓 We invest in your growth through learning budgets, coaching, and stretch opportunities.\n\n🎶 We embrace a creative and dynamic culture, where everyone can play, share, and thrive.\n\n🧘 We believe in work-life harmony — your rhythm matters here.\n\n🏆 We recognize and reward impact, with competitive benefits and clear development paths.\n\nCome join our music-filled workplace, where innovation meets rhythm — and let’s create a magical music experience together.\n\nAmanotes – Where Everyone Can Music.\n\nHow To Apply?\n\nClick the button or contact us at talents@amanotes.com.",
